From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: jrash <johnrash@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 3 Nov 2026 12:28:58 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 264/342] usb_hid: no repeats of any media key but volume up
 and down

7084d089a1 only covered buttons with a bit each. A wireless receiver's media
keys come as an array, and one held for good would keep the screen saver away
just the same, so the rule now goes for every key outside the keyboard page.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 .../input/hid_shared/KeyboardProtocolHandler.cpp   | 14 ++++++--------
 1 file changed, 6 insertions(+), 8 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/input/hid_shared/KeyboardProtocolHandler.cpp b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/input/hid_shared/KeyboardProtocolHandler.cpp
index fb589b5ef2..9cdcc4f928 100644
--- a/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/input/hid_shared/KeyboardProtocolHandler.cpp
+++ b/src/add-ons/kernel/drivers/input/hid_shared/KeyboardProtocolHandler.cpp
@@ -835,14 +835,12 @@ KeyboardProtocolHandler::_ReadReport(bigtime_t timeout, uint32 *cookie)
 			_WriteKey(key, keyDown);
 
 			if (keyDown) {
-				// repeat handling; of the buttons with a bit each (headsets,
-				// USB audio adapters) only volume up and down repeat: such a
-				// button can read as held for good (an adapter's "play"),
-				// and its repeats would count as input for ever, so the
-				// screen saver would never start
-				bool onOffControl = !fKeys[i]->Array()
-					&& fKeys[i]->UsagePage() != B_HID_USAGE_PAGE_KEYBOARD;
-				if (!onOffControl
+				// repeat handling; of the media keys (headsets, USB audio
+				// adapters, wireless receivers) only volume up and down
+				// repeat: such a key can read as held for good (an adapter's
+				// "play"), and its repeats would count as input for ever, so
+				// the screen saver would never start
+				if (fKeys[i]->UsagePage() == B_HID_USAGE_PAGE_KEYBOARD
 					|| key == ((B_HID_USAGE_PAGE_CONSUMER << 16)
 						| B_HID_UID_CON_VOLUME_INCREMENT)
 					|| key == ((B_HID_USAGE_PAGE_CONSUMER << 16)
